# Feature: drop zone (Phase 9)

Library screen `#dropzone`: drop **WAV, AIFF, FLAC, MP3** or folders. Renderer uses `pathForFile` + `statPath`. Only directories and those suffixes go to Python (`isAudioPath` in `app.js`, `AUDIO_EXTS` in `main.js`, `AUDIO_SUFFIXES` in `python/core/audio_formats.py`). Copy in the drop zone is user-facing: no Zoom, no YAMNet. Art: two Material-style **audio file** icons (folded page + note), orange in front and green behind, centered. Closable via the drop zone **X** and `#app-bar` **Show drop zone** / **Hide drop zone**. Last drop: `#ingest-panel` **X** and `#app-bar` **Show last drop** / **Hide last drop** (disabled while ingesting).

`classify_and_ingest {paths}` tags files and **moves or copies** them into `libraryRoot` (`ingestMode`). Same method for reclassify. Load the listening model with `warmup` after the library opens (overlay “Getting ready…”), not on the first drop. Disable further drops while `ingesting` or warming. After the job, set `ingesting = false` **before** `refresh()`.

`#dropzone-progress` is the overall bar (file index + stage / analyze `pct`): solid accent fill, stage label, `1 of n · pct%`. No EQ/soundwave animation. `#ingest-panel` matches the drop zone look (dashed accent border, same light orange/green radial gradient, accent **Last drop** title). Close control is an **X** in the header **flex** row (`margin-left: auto`, not `position: absolute`) so it stays aligned when the job list is empty. `#ingest-jobs` lists per-file status (`inspect` → `analyze` → `tag` → `move` → `done`/`error`). Done rows show **why** (`Speech · 0.82` or `Mixed · nothing reached 0.3`). Failed rows use danger styling; `#ingest-summary` explains a failed or partial drop (do not say “Added 0 files”). Job errors are user-facing (`core.errors.explain` / `friendlyError`). **X** or **Hide last drop** hides the panel after the job (disabled while ingesting). Then `list_library` refresh. Dragging library files out of Fieldy must not re-ingest them if they are dropped back on `#dropzone`. Undo/Redo in `#app-bar` reverse the drop.

Prevent window default drag/drop so Chromium does not navigate. Python walks folders for supported audio; other files in a folder are skipped.
